There are unitary representations $\pi_z:F\to\mathcal B(K)$, indexed by $z\in\mathbb T$, and operators $A_k(g)\in\mathcal B(K)$, indexed by $k\in\mathbb Z$ and $g\in F$, such that $$\begin{aligned}
 \pi_z(g)&=\sum_{k\in\mathbb Z}z^kA_k(g),
 &\sup_{g\in F}\|A_k(g)\|&\leq c_k,
 &c_k&=\mathbf 1_{\{k=0\}}+\frac{2t^{|k|}}{1-t},
 \label{eq:fourier}\\
 \pi_z(s_j)&\xrightarrow[j\to\infty]{\mathrm{WOT}}tzp_e.
 \label{eq:circle-limit}
\end{aligned}$$ The series in <a href="#eq:fourier" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:fourier">[eq:fourier]</a> converges absolutely in operator norm, uniformly in $g$ and $z$, and $$\label{eq:moments}
 S_0:=\sum_{k\in\mathbb Z}c_k<\infty,
 \qquad S_1:=\sum_{k\in\mathbb Z}|k|c_k<\infty.$$

For the algebras in <a href="#eq:algebras" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:algebras">[eq:algebras]</a>, $$\label{eq:near-bound}
 \gamma(M,N)\leq C\|UV-VU\|,
 \qquad
 C:=\sum_{k,m,p,h\in\mathbb Z}
       c_kc_mc_pc_h|m-p|\,|h|<\infty.$$ Moreover, for every $g\in G$, $$\label{eq:group-bound}
 \bigl\|W(\lambda(g)\otimes I_L)W^*
            -\lambda(g)\otimes f(g)\bigr\|
 \leq C\|UV-VU\|.$$ The constant is independent of $D,U,V$.

For each $n$, let $E_{1n},E_{2n}$ be commuting projections on a complex Hilbert space $H_n$, with $D_n=E_nH_n$ nonzero and finite-dimensional, where $E_n=E_{1n}E_{2n}$. Let $\widetilde R_{1n},\widetilde R_{2n}$ be unitaries commuting with both projections, and write $R_{in}=\widetilde R_{in}|_{D_n}$. Suppose $\mathcal A_{1n},\mathcal A_{2n}\subset\mathcal B(H_n)$ are commuting unital von Neumann algebras and there are $T_{in}\in\mathcal A_{in}$ such that $$\label{eq:corner-hypothesis}
 \|T_{in}-E_{in}\widetilde R_{in}\|\longrightarrow0
 \quad(i=1,2).$$ Then, for all sufficiently large $n$, there are commuting unitaries $\widehat R_{1n},\widehat R_{2n}$ on $D_n$ with $$\|\widehat R_{in}-R_{in}\|\longrightarrow0\quad(i=1,2).$$

Let $L$ be a nonzero separable Hilbert space, let $D\subseteq\mathcal B(L)$ be a unital norm-separable $C^*$-algebra with $Z(D)=\mathbb CI_L$, and let $P,Q\subseteq D$ be unital $C^*$-subalgebras containing $I_L$. On $H=\bigoplus_{n\ge1}L$, define $$\label{eq:sequence-definition}
\mathcal E_D(P)=\{(x_n)_{n\ge1}:x_n\in D,\ x_n\to p\in P\text{ in norm}\},$$ and define $\mathcal E_D(Q)$ similarly. Then:*


1.  *These are unital norm-separable $C^*$-algebras with common identity, and $$\label{eq:distance-equality}
    d_{\mathrm{KK}}(\mathcal E_D(P),\mathcal E_D(Q))=d_{\mathrm{KK}}(P,Q).$$*


2.  *If a unitary conjugates $\mathcal E_D(P)$ onto $\mathcal E_D(Q)$, there are unitaries $U_n\in\mathcal B(L)$ with $U_nDU_n^*=D$ such that, for every $b\in Q$, some $p_b\in P$ satisfies $$\label{eq:pointwise-normalizers}
    \left\|b-U_np_bU_n^*\right\|\longrightarrow0.$$ The same sequence $(U_n)$ works for every $b$.*

3.  *The two algebras have the same commutant, and hence the same von Neumann closure.

For every $0<t<1$, there is a unitary representation $\pi_t:G\to\mathcal B(K)$ such that, with $r=\sqrt{1-t^2}$, $$\begin{aligned}
\left\langle \pi_t(s_i)\delta_e,\delta_e\right\rangle&=t\quad(i\ge1),\label{eq:coefficient}\\
\sup_{g\in G}\left\|\pi_t(g)-\lambda(g)\right\|&\le c(t),\qquad
c(t)=2(1-r)+\frac{t}{1-t}+t.\label{eq:uniform}
\end{aligned}$$ In particular, $c(t)\to0$ as $t\downarrow0$.

The algebra $D$ in <a href="#eq:D" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:D">[eq:D]</a> has scalar center, and $$\label{eq:commutant}
D'=\{Y\otimes I_K:Y\in\lambda(G)'\}.$$ There is a unitary $W\in\mathcal B(L)$ such that $$\label{eq:close-W}
WP_0W^*=P_t,\qquad \left\|W-I_L\right\|\le c(t).$$
